{"parentUuid":"04948bb3-de24-4dbc-91c3-89e12aebd493","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/alex/workspace/cli","sessionId":"4b3ddf27-d7f7-4773-b4f2-b94b999c661d","version":"2.1.29","gitBranch":"alex/fix-worktree-shadow-branch-collision","slug":"federated-knitting-lantern","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01GAzbUBqEnhrurVi9F2XN84","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking a good design question. Let me think about this...\n\nCurrently, the shadow branch is named based on the HEAD commit hash: `entire/<commit-hash[:7]>`. This means if two worktrees are at the same commit, they would share the same shadow branch.\n\nWhy would two worktrees be at the same commit?\n1. User creates a new worktree from the same branch/commit\n2. User has multiple worktrees that happen to be at the same point in history\n\nIs there any reason to SHARE the shadow branch between worktrees?\n\nArguments FOR sharing:\n- If the same user is working on the same commit in different terminals/worktrees, maybe they want the checkpoints unified?\n- Less branch proliferation?\n\nArguments AGAINST sharing (and for worktree-specific shadow branches):\n- Worktrees are meant to be isolated workspaces\n- Two different sessions making changes could have conflicting file states\n- The checkpoint data includes file snapshots - mixing two worktrees' file states is confusing\n- The whole point of the conflict error is to PREVENT this sharing\n\nLooking at the current design:\n- Session state files include `worktree_path` to track which worktree they belong to\n- The conflict error exists specifically to prevent cross-worktree collisions\n- The `SessionIDConflictError` also exists to prevent different sessions from using the same shadow branch\n\nSo the design intent seems to be: **each worktree should have its own shadow branch, even if at the same commit**.\n\nBut currently, the shadow branch name is only based on the commit hash, not the worktree. So if we wanted worktree-specific shadow branches, we'd need to include something worktree-specific in the branch name.\n\nOptions:\n1. Include worktree path hash in the shadow branch name: `entire/<commit>-<worktree-hash>`\n2. Include session ID in the shadow branch name: `entire/<commit>-<session-id>`\n3. Keep current naming but handle the conflict more gracefully\n\n\n4. Make shadow branches worktree-specific entirely - each worktree gets its own branch, eliminating conflicts between them. This would mean more branches overall, though they'd be cleaned up on commit anyway. The tradeoff is that someone couldn't intentionally continue a session from a different worktree, but that seems like an uncommon scenario. The error message suggesting users can \"continue the previous session from the original worktree\" implies the design expects sessions to stay within their worktree.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":492,"cache_read_input_tokens":88008,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":492},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CXinQCe8iDPYAwUEoMTcg","type":"assistant","uuid":"a8846a71-157f-4941-810d-8fcdb9987e73","timestamp":"2026-02-02T06:39:45.225Z"}
{"parentUuid":"a8846a71-157f-4941-810d-8fcdb9987e73","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/alex/workspace/cli","sessionId":"4b3ddf27-d7f7-4773-b4f2-b94b999c661d","version":"2.1.29","gitBranch":"alex/fix-worktree-shadow-branch-collision","slug":"federated-knitting-lantern","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01GAzbUBqEnhrurVi9F2XN84","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good question. Let me think about this...\n\n**Current design**: Shadow branch is `entire/<commit-hash>`, so two worktrees at the same commit would share it.\n\n**Why this might be intentional**:\n- Simpler naming scheme\n- If you `cd` between worktrees without starting new sessions, the data is there\n\n**But in practice**:\n- Worktrees are meant to be isolated workspaces\n- Different sessions would have different file states, so mixing them is confusing\n- The conflict error exists precisely to *prevent* sharing\n\nSo honestly... **no, there's no good reason to share**. The conflict detection is a band-aid for a naming scheme that creates unnecessary collisions.\n\nA cleaner solution might be to make shadow branches worktree-specific, like:\n- `entire/<commit>-<worktree-hash>` or\n- `entire/<commit>/<worktree-name>`\n\nThat would eliminate cross-worktree conflicts entirely. Each worktree gets its own shadow branch, no collisions possible.\n\nIs that the direction you're thinking? Or do you want to keep the current naming and just fix the false positive (no checkpoints = no conflict)?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":492,"cache_read_input_tokens":88008,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":492},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CXinQCe8iDPYAwUEoMTcg","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae251316-3a70-459c-9b27-a19aa41e83a0","timestamp":"2026-02-02T06:39:50.549Z"}
